# ar8030-transport-tx runtime configuration, sourced by
# /etc/init.d/S65ar8030-transport-tx.

# AR8030_TRANSPORT_TX_ENABLED=false

# Extra flags passed straight to ar8030-transport-tx -- see its -h output
# (ar8030-transport's README "Build" / tx/main.c usage()) for the full
# list. Example overriding the bb_socket port and bitrate margin:
#   AR8030_TRANSPORT_TX_ARGS="-o 2 -m 0.70 -n 512 -x 20000"
AR8030_TRANSPORT_TX_ARGS=""

# Extra flags passed straight to ar8030-lifecycled -- see its --help
# output (ar8030-transport's README "ar8030-lifecycled: link supervisor
# + bind button" / "HTTP control API" / lifecycled/main.c usage()) for
# the full list. Empty by default -- most boards have no physical bind
# button and the HTTP control API is opt-in. A board that wants either
# should override this in its own overlay copy of this file, e.g.:
#   AR8030_LIFECYCLED_ARGS="--bind-gpio 0 --http-port 8899"
AR8030_LIFECYCLED_ARGS="--bind-gpio 0 --http-port 8899"
